.TH "SOPLOS-REPO-MANAGER" "1" "2026-11-18" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-repo-manager \- build, check and publish APT repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-repo-manager
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-repo-manager
keeps APT repositories made with
.BR reprepro (1),
signed with GPG and published on GitHub, from a graphical interface. Built
with Tauri 2, Rust and Svelte, it joins two programs of the 2.x family, Soplos
Repo Manager and Soplos Packager, and is meant for any APT repository. Its
pages are in five groups:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B Repository:
the repositories (made in an empty folder, with their signing key, title and
Git address) and their packages. Packages are added from files or whole
folders, gone through with every folder inside, to one repository or to
several at once, after a review that says what is new, what is upgraded and
what is already there. The indexes are signed once, the AppStream data that
software centers read is made from the packages themselves, and the change is
published as one commit.
.IP \[bu]
.B Build:
a Debian package made from one program (installed in /usr/bin), from a program
in a folder (installed in /opt with a launcher in /usr/bin) or from a folder
laid out as the system, with its menu entry, its icon and its AppStream
metainfo; and the check of any package before it is published: what
.BR reprepro (1)
and GitHub would refuse, and what software centers need to show it.
.BR lintian (1)
runs only when it is asked for.
.IP \[bu]
.B Team:
the proposals a team sends to a repository as pull requests, accepted (the
packages are added, signed and published) or rejected with a reason, and the
page to send packages for review.
.IP \[bu]
.B Publish:
the destinations proposals are sent to, and the GitHub accounts.
.IP \[bu]
.B Tools:
the GPG keys that sign the repositories (made, imported, exported and backed
up) and the cleanup of a repository: emptying its packages, or also resetting
its Git history to a single commit.
.P
Long jobs (publishing, sending, accepting, checking) show their progress and
the output of git, reprepro and gpg in a bar at the bottom of the window, and
can be cancelled.
.P
GitHub tokens are kept only in the keyring of the system, through the Secret
Service (GNOME Keyring, KWallet, KeePassXC). A token never goes on a command
line, into a URL or into the configuration of a Git repository: git gets it
through its environment and curl through its standard input.
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English. The light or dark theme of the window follows the one of the
desktop.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+1 \fRto\fB Ctrl+9
The first nine pages.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab
Next page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Tab
Previous page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/org.soplos.repomanager/repos.json
The repositories the program knows and the one in use. On the first start it
is made from the profiles of the 2.x version.
.TP
.I ~/.config/org.soplos.repomanager/credentials.json
The list of GitHub accounts and the one in use. The tokens are not in it: they
are in the keyring of the system.
.TP
.I ~/.config/org.soplos.repomanager/maintainer.json
The maintainer of the last package built, offered for the next one.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/org.soplos.repomanager/
Temporary folders used while a package is built or checked; removed when it ends.
